# Commits that changed formatting and nothing else, one full hash per line.
# git blame and GitHub's blame view skip them, so a line is attributed to the
# change that gave it meaning, not to the reformat that moved it.
#
# Add the hash of the commit that first ran a formatter across the
# repository, and of any later formatting-only commit. Keep everything else
# out: a commit that changed behaviour must stay visible in blame.
#
# A formatting-only change goes in its own pull request. Under squash
# merging the branch's commits never reach main; the hash to record is the
# squash commit that lands there, so the next pull request adds it.
#
# GitHub reads this file by name. Locally, run once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs

